<classSpec xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" module="analysis" xml:id="ATTLINGDEP" type="atts" ident="att.linguistic.dependency">
  <desc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">provides attributes for
    annotating dependency relations between word-level elements.</desc>
  <classes/>
  <attList>
    <attDef ident="depN" usage="opt">
      <gloss versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">token index</gloss>
      <desc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">encodes the token index or index
        range of a word-level element in a syntactic dependency relation.</desc>
      <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"><dataRef key="teidata.word"/></datatype>
      <valDesc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">is by convention an
        integer or a hyphen-separated range of integers.</valDesc>
    </attDef>
    <attDef ident="depR" usage="opt">
      <gloss versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">syntactic dependency relation</gloss>
      <desc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">encodes a dependency relation
        between the element bearing this attribute and its syntactic head in
        terms of a pair consisting of the head’s token index and <!-- a label
        for --> the type of the dependency relation.</desc>
      <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"><dataRef key="teidata.text"/></datatype>
      <valDesc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">should use a colon to
        separate the head’s token index and <!-- the label for --> the type of
        the dependency relation.</valDesc>
    </attDef>
    <attDef ident="depE" usage="opt">
      <gloss versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">enhanced syntactic dependency relations</gloss>
      <desc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">encodes enhanced syntactic
        dependency relations between the element bearing this attribute and its
        syntactic heads in terms of a list of pairs each consisting of the
        head’s token index and <!-- a label for --> the type of the dependency
        relation.</desc>
      <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"><dataRef key="teidata.text"/></datatype>
      <valDesc versionDate="2025-12-02" xml:lang="en">should use a colon to
        separate the head’s token index and <!-- the label for --> the type of
        the dependency relation, and a pipe symbol as a list-item separator.</valDesc>
    </attDef>
  </attList>
  <exemplum xml:lang="en">
    <p>Universal Dependency (UD) annotation of the English sentence <mentioned>She buys
    books.</mentioned>.</p>
    <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
      <s>
        <w depN="1" depR="2:nsubj" pos="PRON" lemma="she">She</w>
        <w depN="2" depR="0:root" pos="VERB" lemma="buy">buys</w>
        <w depN="3" depR="2:obj" pos="NOUN" lemma="book" join="right">books</w>
        <pc depN="4" depR="2:punct" pos="PUNCT" lemma=".">.</pc>
      </s>
    </egXML>
  </exemplum>
  <exemplum xml:lang="en">
    <p>Universal Dependency (UD) annotation of the English sentence <mentioned>She buys
    and sells books.</mentioned>.</p>
    <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
      <s>
        <w depN="1" depR="2:nsubj" depE="2:nsubj|4:nsubj" pos="PRON PRP" msd="Case=Nom|Gender=Fem|Number=Sing|Person=3|PronType=Prs" lemma="she">She</w>
        <w depN="2" depR="0:root" depE="0:root" pos="VERB VBZ" msd="Mood=Ind|Number=Sing|Person=3|Tense=Pres|VerbForm=Fin" lemma="buy">buys</w>
        <w depN="3" depR="4:cc" depE="4:cc" pos="CCONJ CC" lemma="and">and</w>
        <w depN="4" depR="2:conj" depE="0:root|2:conj" pos="VERB VBZ" msd="Mood=Ind|Number=Sing|Person=3|Tense=Pres|VerbForm=Fin" lemma="sell">sells</w>
        <w depN="5" depR="2:obj" depE="2:obj|4:obj" pos="NOUN NNS" msd="Number=Plur" lemma="book" join="right">books</w>
        <pc depN="6" depR="2:punct" depE="2:punct" pos="PUNCT ." lemma=".">.</pc>
      </s>
    </egXML>
  </exemplum>
  <exemplum xml:lang="en">
    <p>Universal Dependency (UD) annotation of the German noun phrase <mentioned
    xml:lang="de">ein Hotel zum Wohlfühlen</mentioned>.</p>
    <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
      <phr>
        <w depN="1" depR="2:det" pos="DET" lemma="eine">ein</w>
        <w depN="2" depR="0:root" pos="NOUN" lemma="Hotel">Hotel</w>
        <w depN="3-4" type="surface">zum</w>
        <w depN="3" depR="5:case" pos="ADP" lemma="zu">zu</w>
        <w depN="4" depR="5:det" pos="DET" lemma="die">dem</w>
        <w depN="5" depR="2:nmod" pos="NOUN" lemma="Wohlfühlen">Wohlfühlen</w>
      </phr>
    </egXML>
  </exemplum>
  <remarks xml:lang="en" versionDate="2025-12-02">
    <p>In the UD examples above, a <att>head</att> value of <val>0</val> by
      convention refers to an unrepresented, <soCalled>virtual</soCalled>, root
      node. The corresponding <att>deprel</att> value is <val>root</val>. (For
      discussion, cf. section <ptr target="#AILADEP"/>.)</p>
    <p>The following table summarises the serialisation choices for UD’s CoNLL-U format in TEI XML.
      <table cols="3">
        <row role="label">
          <cell>CoNLL-U column</cell>
          <cell>TEI representation</cell>
          <cell>TEI class</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>ID</code></cell>
          <cell><att>depN</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.global</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>FORM</code></cell>
          <cell><gi>w</gi> or <gi>pc</gi> content</cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">model.segLike</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>LEMMA</code></cell>
          <cell><att>lemma</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>UPOS</code></cell>
          <cell><att>pos</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>XPOS</code></cell>
          <cell>additional list item in <att>pos</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>FEATS</code></cell>
          <cell><att>msd</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>HEAD</code></cell>
          <cell><att>depR</att>, part before <code>:</code></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic.dependency</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>DEPREL</code></cell>
          <cell><att>depR</att>, part after <code>:</code></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic.dependency</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>DEPS</code></cell>
          <cell><att>depE</att></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic.dependency</ident></cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell><code>SpaceAfter=No</code> in <code>MISC</code></cell>
          <cell><att>join</att> with value <val>right</val></cell>
          <cell><ident type="class">att.linguistic</ident></cell>
        </row>
      </table>
    </p>
  </remarks>
  <listRef>
    <ptr target="#AILADEP"/>
  </listRef>
</classSpec>
